  "text": ".charCodeAt(user_input)\n.charCodeAt(\"user_input\")\n\nx, y, z = 1, -1, 0\nS = x+y+z\nW = x*y+z\nK = x*y*z\nP = S*x + W*y + K*z\nU = 1/K\nd1 = y-x\nd2 = z-x\nd3 = y-z\ny1 = P - W/{x} - P*z\nx2 = y1*d1 + X*d3\nD9 = x2-i*y/d1 + U*y1\nd123 = d1*x + d3*z\n\n### Making x, y, z distinct\n\nNow consider the case where $x, y, z$ are distinct.\n\nSince $|x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352$ and knowing that the roots of $Q(z) = z^3 + sz + t$ are $x, y, z$, we have:\n\n\\[ x + y + z = 0 \\]\n\\[ xy + yz + zx = s \\]\n\\[ x y z = -t \\]\n\nSince $|x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352$, and given that $|x|^2, |y|^2, |z|^2$ are the squared magnitudes of the roots, we can write:\n\n\\[ (x + y + z)^2 = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 2(xy + yz + zx) \\]\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 352$. So,\n\n\\[ |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352 \\]\n\\[ (x + y + z)^2 = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 2(x y + y z + z x) \\]\n\\[ 0 = 352 + 2(xy + yz + zx) \\]\n\\[ xy + yz + zx = -176 \\]\n\nSince $x + y + z = 0$, the roots form an equilateral triangle in the complex plane. This implies that the distances between any two of these roots are equal. The only choice for distinct roots of $Q(z)$ that satisfies this condition is $x = 1, y = i, z = -1$, which should result in a symmetric equilateral triangle. \n\nTherefore, the sides of the equilateral triangle are:\n\n\\[ |x - y| = |1 - i| \\]\n\\[ |x - z| = |1 - (-1)| = 2 \\]\n\\[ |y - z| = |i - (-1)| \\]\n\nCalculating these distances, we get:\n\n\\[ |1 - i| = \\sqrt{1^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{2} \\]\n\\[ |1 - (-1)| = 2 \\]\n\\[ |i - (-1)| = \\sqrt{1^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nThus, the sides of the equilateral triangle are $\\sqrt{2}$, $\\sqrt{2}$, and $2$. The base $b$ of the triangle is $2$, so:\n\n\\[ b^2 = 4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is\n\n\\(\\boxed{4}\\)\nQ.E.D.",
